  "notes": "B.S. Computer Science, College of Science and Engineering. QUARTER SYSTEM — all credits are quarter hours. Built from the official WWU Computer Science department sample 4-year plan (https://cs.wwu.edu/plan-study, 'Computer Science, BS Catalog 2025-26'). Major sequence: CSCI 141/145/201/247/305/330/347/345/401/367/405/447, CISS 346 (Secure Software Development, required before senior project), MATH 124/125/204/341, one lab-science series (PHYS 161/162/163), senior project CSCI 491/492/493 (or 490), 4 CS electives. Admission to the major is based on performance in CSCI 201/247/305. GURs: QSR and LSCI/SCI satisfied by major (MATH 124/125, PHYS series); remaining GURs (ACOM ENG 101, BCOM, HUM 12cr+, SSC 12cr+, ACGM, BCGM) modeled as choice slots; upper-division writing proficiency points and 60 upper-division credits satisfied within the plan. Senior project credits (4 each) use the WWU 400-level standard; CS elective credits (4 each) per department standard. 180 quarter credits total.",
